---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { breadcrumb, webPage } from '../data/schema';
const path = '/accessibility/';
const title = `Accessibility | ${site.name}`;
const description = `How ${site.name} works to make this website usable for everyone, and how to tell us about a problem.`;
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} schema={[webPage(path, title, description), breadcrumb([['Home', '/'], ['Accessibility', path]])]}>
  <section class="section wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Accessibility</p>
    <h1>Built to be <em>usable by everyone.</em></h1>
    <p class="mono updated">Last reviewed: October 2026</p>
    <p>We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA. We reviewed this website against those guidelines in October 2026 and are fixing problems as we find them. It has not yet had an independent accessibility audit. What is in place today:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A “Skip to content” link and full keyboard navigation, with a visible focus outline.</li>
      <li>Labeled form fields with error messages announced to screen readers.</li>
      <li>Reduced motion when your device asks for it.</li>
      <li>Text alternatives for photos and floor plan images, plus bedroom, bathroom and square-foot details on every plan page.</li>
      <li>A written room-by-room description of the layout on the <a href="/floor-plans/sunset-retreat/">Sunset Retreat Model</a> page, beside its blueprint.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Known limitations</h2>
    <p>The floor plan PDFs you can download from each plan page are scanned images without text, so screen readers cannot read them. Only the Sunset Retreat Model page has a written description of its layout so far. For any other plan, or for room sizes, tell us which plan and we will get you the information another way (see below).</p>
    <h2>Found a problem?</h2>
    <p>Tell us what page and what happened, and we’ll fix it or get you the information another way. Call <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .prose { max-width: 760px; } .prose ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; } .prose a { color: var(--clay); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  .updated { font-size: .75rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-top: 2.2rem; }
</style>
